{
  "$comment": "Microcopy in Curve's components: every text a component shows or reads out by default. `text` holds the text per language (`en` is the default, `nl` the Dutch translation); this package's build turns it into `dist/index.ts`, which both component packages copy and use, so this file is the only place a default lives. Apps pick a language with `CurveMicrocopyProvider` (React) or `provideCurveMicrocopy()` (Angular). Per framework: `where` is the component, `change` how an app changes one text (null: only through the language). Entries with `example: true` describe a format (a function), not a text: their texts only show sample output and are not generated. Documented in Storybook under Foundations > Microcopy and Curve > Voor developers > Microcopy. Placeholders like {requiredLength} are filled in at runtime.",
  "entries": {
    "field.label.optional": {
      "component": "Field",
      "kind": "zichtbaar",
      "description": "Achter het label van een optioneel veld (`hlmField optional` / `<Field optional>`).",
